# LF in every checkout, on every platform. Git for Windows (and the
# windows-latest CI runner) defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would
# check sources, fixtures and the OpenClaw bundle out with CRLF - bytes the
# suite never ran against. Binary files are still detected and left alone.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows launchers must keep CRLF: cmd.exe misparses labels and blocks in
# LF-only batch files.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
